@*
    The owned modal frame (design handoff § New entry wizard): backdrop + a .wide .blueprint
    panel wearing its four corner registration marks. Fluent's dialog provider is gone, so
    the accessibility it carried is owned here: role=dialog + aria-modal, focus trapped via
    console.js (restored on close), Escape and a backdrop click cancel.

    Structure rule (measured, 2026-08-10): the panel must NOT be the scroll container. The
    corner marks sit 6px outside the frame by design, so a scrolling .wide permanently
    "overflows" by 6px both axes and its auto scrollbars flip on every re-render — the
    per-keystroke scrollbar flicker. The title and actions stay pinned on the frame; only
    .dbody scrolls, and it contains nothing absolutely positioned.

    Escape lives in the JS focus trap, not a Blazor @onkeydown: a backdrop key handler
    turns every keystroke in every field into a server round-trip and re-render.

    DNs never render in the title (one unbreakable token whose min-content width grows with
    tree depth — docs/findings.md); callers put them in body markup with word-break.
*@
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime Js

<div class="dialog-backdrop" @onclick="Cancel">
    <div class="wide blueprint" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="@Title"
         tabindex="-1" @ref="_panel" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
        <i class="corner tl"></i><i class="corner tr"></i><i class="corner bl"></i><i class="corner br"></i>
        <div class="dialog-title">@Title</div>
        <div class="dbody">@ChildContent</div>
        <div class="dialog-actions">@Actions</div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public required string Title { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? Actions { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised on Escape or a backdrop click; the owner closes the dialog.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnCancel { get; set; }

    private ElementReference _panel;
    private IJSObjectReference? _module;
    private DotNetObjectReference<ConsoleDialog>? _self;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            _self = DotNetObjectReference.Create(this);
            _module = await Js.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/console.js");
            await _module.InvokeVoidAsync("trapFocus", _panel, _self);
        }
    }

    private Task Cancel() => OnCancel.InvokeAsync();

    /// <summary>Called by the focus trap when Escape is pressed inside the dialog.</summary>
    [JSInvokable]
    public Task CancelFromJs() => Cancel();

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        if (_module is not null)
        {
            try
            {
                await _module.InvokeVoidAsync("releaseFocus");
                await _module.DisposeAsync();
            }
            catch (JSDisconnectedException)
            {
                // Circuit gone; nothing to release.
            }
        }
        _self?.Dispose();
    }
}
